# Degree ninety-seven: the largest exponents in the range

`n = 97` is odd, so the odd-degree bound needs moments at `k = 46` and `k = 47`, and `k = 47`
is the largest exponent occurring anywhere in `5 ≤ n ≤ 97`.  As in degree fifty-three,
nothing here computes `qrow`; the kernel performs one integer exponentiation per moment (to
8.5 and 9.1 million bits) and reads the row back off.
